            "tender": {
                "id": "CF-1986500D0O000000rwimUAA",
                "title": "Agile Foundation and Practitioner Training",
                "description": "Agile culture is about creating an environment that is underpinned by values, behaviours and practices which enable organisations, teams and individuals to be more adaptive, flexible, innovative and resilient when dealing with complexity, uncertainty and change. \r\n\r\n(Based on the works of Ed Schein, Frederick Laloux, Vlatka Hlupic, Peter Senge and Alan Furlong) \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nAgile ways of working are vitally important to the success of the DAS Group, encouraging innovation, collaboration and adaptability to change and this training opportunity provides colleagues the training to: \r\n\r\nunderstand and be able to articulate the benefits of an Agile approach to project management \r\n\r\nbe able to operate as a project manager in an Agile environment.",
